    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "HAWAII\nAloha!\nPLEASE BE OUR GUEST:\nWHISKIES\nBOURBON\nSCOTCH\nCANADIAN\nCOCKTAILS\nUNITED AIR LINES SPECIAL\nVERY DRY MARTINI (GIN OR VODKA)\nOLD FASHIONED\nMANHATTAN\nDAIQUIRI\nBLOODY MARY\nSPANISH SHERRY\nMAI TAI\nGIN\nVODKA\nBEER\nTOMATO JUICE\nPINEAPPLE JUICE\nSOFT BEVERAGES\n* * *\nHAWAIIAN MACADAMIA NUTS\nLIQUEURS\nCREME DE MENTHE\nCOGNAC\nDRAMBUIE\nBENEDICTINE AND BRANDY\nBLACK RUSSIAN\nHAWAIIAN LIQUEUR\nPapaaina\n(MENU)\nAPPETIZER\nCREAMED MUSHROOMS ON TOAST\nPUREE OF GREEN PEA SOUP OR CONSOMME au SHERRY\nWAFERS\nBROILED NEW YORK CUT SIRLOIN STEAK, FINES HERBES SAUCE OR\nBAKED BREAST OF CHICKEN a la FLORENTINE, FINES HERBES SAUCE OR\nVEAL SCALLOPINI MARSALA OR\nSHRIMP PROVENCALE\nMAINLINER BAKED POTATO\nGREEN PEAS WITH TOMATOES\nROLLS\nASSORTED DINNER ROLLS\nSALADS\nHEART OF BUTTER LETTUCE SALAD OR PRINCESS KAIULANI SALAD\nBLEU CHEESE DRESSING OR FRENCH DRESSING\nDESSERTS\nHOT FUDGE SUNDAE,\nCOUPE NIPPON, BISCUIT TORTONI\nOR PETITS FOURS\nBEVERAGES\nCOFFEE\nDINNER MINT\nSANKA\nTEA MILK\nTHE WINES SERVED WITH THIS MENU ARE\nBEAUJOLAIS ST. VINCENT, CHAMPAGNE AND EMERALD DRY.\nThis menu prepared in United Air Lines Flight Kitchen at Honolulu, Alfred Rigert, Chef.\nPresident, Chefs de Cuisine, Hawaii, Member, American Culinary Federation\nU. S. Department of Agriculture Regulations prohibit use of certain fruits and vegetables in natural or raw state on all fights from Hawaii to the Mainland."
    ],
